Chapter: EffectHandlerClause
  cites Foreword chapter Console

 Adversarial probe (effect rows stage 0). Handler-clause
 laundering: a def declared pure handles Reader, and the ask CLAUSE
 performs Console I/O. Handler typing strips the handled effect
 from the body but the clauses' own effects must surface in the
 result row. Effect rows stage 3b infers clause bodies and unions
 their rows into the handle expression's ambient (the section 7
 rule), so the undeclared clause effect dies at the def boundary
 (CDX2031, with CDX2033 at the let binding). This test is the
 enforcement's regression guard.

Section: Effects

  effect Reader where
    ask : [Reader] Integer

Section: Definitions

  quiet : Integer -> Integer
  quiet (n) =
   let r = with Reader ask
     ask (resume) = act
       print-line-uni "clause side channel"
       resume n
     end
   in r

  opening : [Console] Nothing = act
    print-line-uni ("result " & show (quiet 41))
  end
